      "writtenOn": "2023-04-07T21:13:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My main use case for hashing spans was to have types used as keys to hash maps, but they are very often a struct that wraps the span. This was a fairly light weight way of using the span hashing behavior without requiring a custom Hash struct and additional template arg to SkTHashMap.\n\nA reasonable alternative would be if we declared a hash wrapper template:\n\n    template\u003cE\u003e\n    struct AsSpan {\n        template \u003ctypename K\u003e\n        uint32_t operator()(const K\u0026 k) const {\n            return SkGoodHash()(SkSpan\u003cE\u003e{k});\n        }\n    };\n    \nThe `span_view` declaration lets the wrapping type control its hash, whereas the `Hash` trait wrapper requires users of the span-wrapper know to adjust their maps.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 59,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 64,
        "endChar": 84
      },
      "revId": "8ae63d9f23838c54ea5aa9f54517e5b2c23995ac",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1cc45dd1_0105bba2",
        "filename": "include/private/SkChecksum.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 64,
      "author": {
        "id": 11059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-07T23:37:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think the alternative might be better. The `has_span_view` impl is pretty intimidating. It looks like the example on the cppreference page on `std::void_t`, and I think it\u0027s correct, but at first glance it\u0027s very hard to reason about unless you have seen something similar before. I don\u0027t know if it is worth the complexity vs just having an `AsSpan` class which makes the behavior explicit at the call site. \n\n(Caveat: we need clean, visible failure if you forget `AsSpan`... if it\u0027ll silently do the wrong thing, that\u0027s worse)",
      "parentUuid": "1f04e19c_4381509c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 59,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 64,
        "endChar": 84
      },
      "revId": "8ae63d9f23838c54ea5aa9f54517e5b2c23995ac",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b0929883_a05fc575",
        "filename": "include/private/SkChecksum.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 64,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
